# --- How the booth says the names no dictionary carries. One per line: the word, then
# --- its phonemes in ORACLE's alphabet (CMUdict's, with * before the stressed vowel
# --- and AX for schwa). Each spoken line carries the ones it uses; anything not here
# --- comes from the dictionary or, failing that, the letter rules, which is how
# --- "Oyelaran" was said "OY-uh-luh-ruhn". A broadcaster's reading, not the
# --- language's: a booth anglicises. Add a line when you add a name. ---------------
::say
adebayo      AA D EH B * AY OW
aitkenhead   * EY T K AX N HH EH D
alferov      * AE L F ER AA F
amankwah     AA M * AA NG K W AA
bergqvist    B * ER G K V IH S T
bhandari     B AA N D * AA R IY
